    "intro_html":  "Johnny Marzetti is the church-basement casserole that fed half the Midwest for a century, and it still earns its spot: beefy tomato sauce, wide egg noodles, mushrooms, olives, and a melted cheddar lid. Every bowl brings \u003cstrong\u003e38 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$2.68\u003c/strong\u003e. Comfort food that respects your budget is rare. This is one of them.",
